What fixed the reflow issue specifically:

DataGrid handles virtualization natively — safe for lakhs of rows since it only renders visible rows, unlike the card list which would mount every row into the DOM.
TABLE_AREA_HEIGHT = 600 on the wrapping Paper — this height is constant no matter how many rows are on the page, so the panel never grows or shrinks.
Fixed rowHeight (52px) — every row is the same height, no variable card padding.
Fixed LinearProgress slot (height: 4 wrapper) — the loading bar no longer pushes content up/down when it appears/disappears.
GridEmptyOverlay renders inside the same fixed-height panel for both the "not searched yet" and "no results" states, instead of swapping the whole layout in and out.
Replaced Grid item xs={...} md={...} with the new Grid size={{ xs: ..., md: ... }} API throughout.
